{#
  DIRECTION CONTRACT
  THESIS: The glossary reads as the platform's own reference library, not a
  bolted-on wiki page — homepage-v2's navy/green/glass system carries a
  browse-and-define task the same way it already carries /resources/.
  OWN-WORLD: #F8FAFC/white ground, #76B900 the one accent (active filter
  state, category badges, CTA), navy-950 dark card for the closing CTA banner,
  mono uppercase eyebrows/labels, rounded-2xl glass-tinted term cards
  (border-white/60, gradient sky-100/60 via sky-50/25 to white/50,
  backdrop-blur-sm, shadow-subtle), Inter at homepage-v2 weights.
  STORY: visitor scans the intro, filters by category or reads the whole
  list, opens a term, and converts on a CTA that matches the rest of the site.
  FIRST VIEWPORT: left-aligned "AI Glossary" eyebrow + H1 + subhead over a
  sticky category filter — same structural rhythm as /resources/.
  FORM: extend the established homepage-v2/resources world onto the glossary
  index — content, data bindings, and filter logic inherited, filter state
  unified into a single Alpine scope so category filtering actually drives
  the grid (previously split across two disconnected x-data scopes), no new
  visual system invented.
#}

{% include "partials/navbar-v2.njk" %}

<script>
  document.documentElement.classList.add('js-reveal-hidden');
</script>
<style>
  .js-reveal-hidden [data-reveal]:not(.revealed),
  .js-reveal-hidden [data-reveal-stagger]:not(.revealed) > * {
